WEBVTT

00:00:58.471 --> 00:01:00.556
that are no bigger 
than your little finger.

00:01:00.556 --> 00:01:02.558
In many ways, the sheer size of krill

00:01:02.558 --> 00:01:05.436
seems to have driven 
the evolution of the blue whale.

00:01:08.022 --> 00:01:11.818
See, krill are so small
but are found in dense patches.

00:01:11.984 --> 00:01:13.486
For increased efficiency,

00:01:13.486 --> 00:01:17.156
blue whales have evolved to use 
a feeding strategy called lunge feeding.

00:01:17.865 --> 00:01:20.827
Basically, 
the whale accelerates towards a prey patch

00:01:20.827 --> 00:01:22.578
and opens its mouth wide.

00:01:23.037 --> 00:01:26.040
To increase the capacity, 
its mouth expands.

00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:28.167
The special, accordion-like 
blubber layer

00:01:28.167 --> 00:01:30.711
that extends from its snout 
to its belly button